+
+# Tags on posts
+
+## Context
+
+Readers could not find posts on a topic: the list was one long feed. Product
+asked for author-supplied tags, shown wherever a post appears, with a click
+leading to the posts carrying that tag. Topic pages and a tag cloud will be
+built on the same data, so its shape is a contract other work relies on.
+
+## Decision
+
+- Table `tags` (`id`, `name` unique, case-sensitive) and pivot `post_tags`
+  (`post_id`, `tag_id`), one row per attachment. Models `Tag` and `PostTag`;
+  `Post.tags` is a `belongsToMany` through the pivot.
+- The form field is `tags`: one comma-separated text input on the create and
+  edit forms (an array of names is accepted too). Names are trimmed, empties
+  dropped, duplicates collapsed; then each name must be 1–30 characters and a
+  post carries at most 5. Violations are a 422 on the `tags` field, exactly as
+  an empty title, and nothing is written.
+- Saving syncs the post's tag set: unknown names become tags, listed names are
+  attached, removed names are detached. Unused tags stay in `tags`.
+- Every post object handed to `posts/Index` (`data`) and `posts/Show` (`post`)
+  carries `tags: string[]`, the names sorted alphabetically, `[]` when none.
+- `/posts?tag=<name>` filters the list, newest first, paginated like the
+  unfiltered list; page links keep the filter. An unknown tag lists nothing.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Topic pages and a tag cloud can query `tags` and `post_tags` directly and
+  reuse the `PostResource` shape without a new endpoint.
+- Deleting a post removes its pivot rows explicitly, so it works whether or
+  not the SQLite `foreign_keys` pragma is on.
+- There is no tag garbage collection; a later job may prune tags with no rows
+  in `post_tags`.
